 think it's genuinely true and relevant, not because I need it to win the argument — I'd hold the same position on the core cleanliness claim even without any historical explanation for why it spread. So, to be direct: I'm not asking you to believe in a hidden plot. I'm asking you to notice that "widely believed" and "historically explicable" and "still not demonstrated to be true" can all be the case at once.
